---
import Legal from "../../layouts/Legal.astro"
import Fact from "../../components/Fact.astro"
import { sourceUrl } from "../../site"

const sections: [string, string][] = [
  ["agreement", "Agreement"],
  ["accounts", "Accounts"],
  ["service", "The service"],
  ["content", "Your content"],
  ["payment", "Plans and payment"],
  ["termination", "Suspension and termination"],
  ["open-source", "Open source"],
  ["warranty", "No warranty"],
  ["liability", "Liability"],
  ["indemnity", "Indemnity"],
  ["law", "Law and disputes"],
  ["changes", "Changes"],
  ["general", "General"],
  ["contact", "Contact"],
]
---

<Legal slug="terms" description="The agreement between you and Paperboat for the hosted service: accounts, plans, payment, suspension and liability." {sections}>
  <p slot="intro">
    These terms are the agreement between you and Paperboat (“we”, “us”) for the hosted Paperboat service. Paperboat is operated by
    <Fact name="operators" />.
  </p>

  <section id="agreement">
    <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        By creating an account or paying for a plan, you accept these terms, the <a href="/legal/acceptable-use/">Acceptable Use Policy</a>
        and the <a href="/legal/refunds/">Refund Policy</a>. The <a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> covers personal data, and the
        <a href="/legal/dpa/">Data Processing Addendum</a> applies where data protection law requires one. These terms take effect on
        <Fact name="effective" />. If you accept them for an organisation, you confirm you may bind it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="accounts">
    <h2>2. Accounts</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <ul>
        <li>You must be at least 16, and an adult to buy a paid plan.</li>
        <li>One account is for one person. People who work together use a team; its owner manages members, access and seats.</li>
        <li>You are responsible for everything done with your account, machines, tokens and keys. Tell us at once if someone else has access.</li>
        <li>
          You may not use Paperboat if you are subject to UN, EU, UK or US sanctions, or are in a sanctioned place. Breaking this is a material
          breach.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="service">
    <h2>3. The service</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Traffic between your machines is end-to-end encrypted. Public previews and tunnels are not: HTTPS ends at our edge. See
        <a href="/security/">Security</a>. We do not guarantee availability. We may change features; if a change removes something you pay
        for, we tell you first and you may cancel. Beta features may change or end without notice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Plans have limits, and traffic through our relays and edges has a monthly fair-use amount, then a slower rate. Both are on the
        <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a> and in the <a href="/legal/acceptable-use/#fair-use">Acceptable Use Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="content">
    <h2>4. Your content</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        What is on your machines and what you send or publish stays yours. You give us only the permission needed to run the service and act on
        abuse. You are responsible for what you run and publish, and for having the right to publish it. We do not use your content to train AI
        models. We may use feedback you give us freely.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="payment">
    <h2>5. Plans and payment</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <ul>
        <li>Prices are on the pricing page and in the console. Stripe takes payment. Taxes are added where required.</li>
        <li>Paid plans renew automatically until you cancel. Cancelling in the console stops the next renewal; the plan runs to the end of the paid period.</li>
        <li>We email you at least 30 days before a price increase, which applies from your next renewal.</li>
        <li>Added seats are charged at once for the rest of the period. Removed seats stay paid until the next billing date.</li>
        <li>Payments are not refunded; see the <a href="/legal/refunds/">Refund Policy</a>.</li>
        <li>If a payment stays unpaid 7 days after it fails, the workspace moves to the Free plan's limits.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="termination">
    <h2>6. Suspension and termination</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>You can cancel, remove machines or delete your account at any time in the console. Deletion is immediate and final.</p>
      <p>
        We may block a link, suspend or close an account if you break these terms or the Acceptable Use Policy, put others at risk, dispute a
        valid charge, or the law requires it. We warn you first where we can. We may also close an account or stop the service without cause on
        30 days' notice, and then refund the unused prepaid part.
      </p>
      <p>Sections 4 to 11, and payments already due, survive termination.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="open-source">
    <h2>7. Open source</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The source code at <a href={sourceUrl} rel="noopener">{sourceUrl.replace("https://", "")}</a> is governed by its licences (MIT and
        AGPL-3.0), not these terms. The Paperboat name and logo are ours.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="warranty">
    <h2>8. No warranty</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        To the extent the law allows, the service is provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, including fitness for
        a purpose or uninterrupted, error-free or secure operation. Back up what matters to you. If you lose your ENV master password and
        recovery code, we cannot recover your values.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="liability">
    <h2>9. Liability</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>To the extent the law allows:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Neither side is liable for indirect or consequential loss, or for lost profits, revenue, data or goodwill.</li>
        <li>Each side's total liability is limited to the greater of what you paid us in the 12 months before the claim and US $100.</li>
        <li>These limits do not apply to your payment obligations, your indemnity, fraud, gross negligence, intent, or death or injury caused by negligence.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="indemnity">
    <h2>10. Indemnity</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        You will cover our reasonable costs and liabilities from third-party claims about what you ran or published through Paperboat, or about
        your breach of these terms. This does not apply to consumers where the law forbids it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="law">
    <h2>11. Law and disputes</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the law of <Fact name="law" />. Disputes go to <Fact name="courts" />. Consumers keep the mandatory
        protections and courts of the country where they live.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>12. Changes</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        We email you at least 30 days before a material change takes effect, unless law or security requires sooner. If you do not agree,
        cancel before then.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="general">
    <h2>13. General</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <ul>
        <li>You may not transfer these terms without our consent. We may transfer them to a successor of the service and will email you if we do.</li>
        <li>These terms and the policies they name are the whole agreement. An unenforceable part does not affect the rest. Not enforcing a right is not a waiver.</li>
        <li>Neither side is responsible for events outside its reasonable control.</li>
        <li>You agree to receive notices electronically, by email or in the console.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2>14. Contact</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Paperboat, operated by <Fact name="operators" />. <Fact name="address" />. <Fact name="legalEmail" />.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Legal>
